              "textField": "The main clinical uses of alpha 1 agonists can be predicted by the location of the actual receptors. Since the alpha 1 receptor is on the peripheral blood vessels of the nasal passages and eyes, they are used as *decongestants*, and include *oxymetazoline* which is only available as a nasal spray and *phenylephrine* which is no better than placebo in most clinical trials. Systemically they can be used as *antihypotensives* for people with orthostatic hypotension. They are also used in minor surgery as *blood vessel constrictors*"
